01$) lies just above the V1 mean ($0.798$), while the higher V3 seed ($0.899$) lies above the V2 mean ($0.828$). With two seeds per configuration, the seed-to-seed spreads ($0.051$, $0.043$, $0.098$) are no smaller than the differences between configuration means ($0.031$, $0.022$), so no ordering of the configurations is supported.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"0\\.030\\|memorization capacity\" paper.tex; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('derived/resolution.json'));print(json.dumps(d['search'],indent=0)[:1500])\nc=json.load(open('claims_grounding.json'))['claims']\nfor i in (0,14,18): print(i,c[i])\nE\nls source_evidence source_evidence/search_variants"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":54989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cdd964e4-3ba4-4c45-969d-584fa83d6aeb","uuid":"85fff599-de01-4f57-a1d6-903017de1e31","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:49:29.598Z","request_id":"req_011CgwKsBpuZ4QuGv6d2CsMf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D6RQ6qwbUc3zNUq6eeYb34","type":"tool_result","content":"235:\\paragraph{Relation to the explanations of grokking.} Each account in Section~\\ref{sec:related} associates the delay with a quantity that can depend on width or parametrization: memorization capacity (how early the training split is fitted), initial weight norm and the loss landscape, the relative efficiency of memorizing and generalizing circuits, and the position on the lazy-to-rich axis. The evaluated model touches the last two knobs directly: its initial weights are shrunk by half, which the source comments describe as aimed at reducing lazy-regime memorization, and its multipliers change how large a step each layer takes at a given width. A clear width slope from this model could therefore reflect the multipliers rather than width alone, and a flat slope could reflect their compensating a stock-model dependence. This is why the isolating comparison with a matched stock model (Section~\\ref{sec:discussion}, item iv) matters more than a further estimate of the slope for the evaluated model alone.\n{\n\"modulus\": 53,\n\"train_fraction\": 0.5,\n\"widths\": [\n32,\n64,\n128\n],\n\"max_steps\": 6000,\n\"probe_every\": 300,\n\"seeds\": [\n101,\n102\n],\n\"variants\": [\n{\n\"variant\": 1,\n\"score\": 0.7976868327402136,\n\"final_val_acc_mean\": 0.9805456702253854,\n\"censored_fraction\": 0.6666666666666666,\n\"n_censored_runs\": 4,\n\"n_runs\": 6,\n\"seed_scores\": {\n\"101\": 0.7720297184241743,\n\"102\": 0.8233439470562528\n},\n\"control_max_val_acc\": 0.022775800711743774\n},\n{\n\"variant\": 2,\n\"score\": 0.828466629206468,\n\"final_val_acc_mean\": 0.9443653618030842,\n\"censored_fraction\": 1.0,\n\"n_censored_runs\": 6,\n\"n_runs\": 6,\n\"seed_scores\": {\n\"101\": 0.8069176499968783,\n\"102\": 0.8500156084160579\n},\n\"control_max_val_acc\": 0.02206405693950178\n},\n{\n\"variant\": 3,\n\"score\": 0.8501467191109446,\n\"final_