I fixed all four listed errors (three audit findings plus the manifest schema failure) and the paper recompiles. The repo's figure-manifest validator wouldn't run in this workspace, so I haven't confirmed the schema fix against it.

- **Abstract:**
  - I replaced "calibrated non-answer" with "valid but inconclusive measurement". It now says the interval comes from four seed clusters and its coverage isn't guaranteed.
  - I removed the claim that width dependence "has received little systematic measurement".
  - The Related Work paragraph that lists the explanations of grokking no longer attributes memorization capacity to a cited account. The Related Work gap statement was already hedged, so I left it as is.
- **Development-plane wording:**
  - The text now says the lower V3 seed (0.801) lies just above the V1 mean (0.798), and the higher seed (0.899) lies above the V2 mean (0.828).
  - The first mean difference is corrected to 0.031.
  - "Same size" is now "no larger than the seed-to-seed spreads".
  - The two claims that cover these numbers now name `source_evidence/search_variants/variant*_metrics.json` and `derived/resolution.json`. Those are named in the claim text only; the claims' `source_ids` still point to `result.improvement_001`–`003`.
  - I also added a claim recording the bootstrap-coverage caveat.
- **Figure manifest:** the interval plot and the search-variants dot plot used `figure_type` values the schema doesn't allow. Both are now `scatter`.

The scientific-evidence verifier reports 0 dangling references. `paper.tex` compiles to 14 pages with no undefined references. I didn't re-check the body-page budget, so please confirm the 8–9 page limit when you revalidate. I appended this repair to `memory.md` and the global memory files.
